<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Software-stop registry liveness pager — S-FRAC stage-3 ops (#471 operator
  shortlist item 2: "pager scheduled nowhere, page never test-fired").

  Runs scripts/stops_liveness_pager.sh every 10 minutes. The wrapper invokes
  the EXECUTION-repo liveness checker (renquant_execution.software_stops_liveness,
  renquant-execution#29 — moved out of the deprecated umbrella per the
  Codex review of this package's prior revision), resolving the pinned
  execution/pipeline/common checkouts through the R-PIN Stage-1 runtime
  inventory (~/.renquant/deploy/runtime-inventory.json, read via
  renquant_orchestrator.deployment_manifest.load_runtime_inventory — the
  neutral per-host repo-name to checkout-path map, no umbrella lock-file
  dependency), and pages the LIVE ops ntfy topic on STALE / CORRUPT /
  checker-crash / inventory-resolution failure. The checker
  itself returns OK off-session, so a simple all-day StartInterval is the
  robust schedule: market-hours gating lives in ONE place (the checker),
  not duplicated here.

  TEMPLATE ONLY: merging this file does NOT install anything. Arming is a
  separately-granted operator landing step (the "apply" flag is two hyphens;
  XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen):

      scripts/install_stops_pager.sh install [apply flag]
      scripts/install_stops_pager.sh test-fire STALE   (delivery + response drill)

  ENABLEMENT PREREQUISITES (both must pass before arming):

  (1) WRITER MIGRATION: the sell-only loop must be migrated to stamp the
      registry file at the neutral runtime-state root
      (~/.renquant/runtime/software-stops/) via a separate R-PIN landing
      change. Until then, the checker finds no file and correctly reports
      STALE. Code resolution already goes through R-PIN (this package);
      DATA resolution is the remaining gap.
  (2) SLA DRILL: the alert-latency envelope is ~18 to 28 minutes after
      the first missed pass. Before arming, run a test-fire drill
      (scripts/stops_liveness_pager.sh test-fire STALE) and either
      configure max_staleness_minutes to meet the 15-minute target, or
      obtain explicit operator acceptance of the measured envelope.

  Neither gap blocks MERGING this template (no umbrella dependency remains
  in committed configuration). Both block ARMING/INSTALLING.

  2026-08-29 (fractional dependency chain, step 5 - PREPARATION, orch#1077):
  * ProgramArguments now runs the wrapper from the PINNED run checkout
    (/Users/renhao/git/github/renquant-orchestrator-run/scripts/), the same
    checkout every other manifested com.renquant.* job executes from - never
    the dev working tree, whose branch is whatever the operator last checked
    out.
  * NOT yet declared in ops/launchd_manifest.json, deliberately (Codex on
    orch#1077): a manifested-but-uninstalled job makes the daily run-surface
    drift scan page the ops topic every day until install - a standing false
    positive on the channel that must carry real stop-liveness failures. The
    manifest entry lands in the LANDING PR together with
    `scripts/install_stops_pager.sh install [apply flag]` and the test-fire,
    in one controlled window, gated on (1) the registry writer stamping the
    neutral data root (orchestrator seeder PR in flight) and (2) the SLA
    decision below. install_stops_pager.sh refuses (exit 4) to arm a plist
    that is not manifested or disagrees with its manifest entry.
  * SLA: NOT SATISFIED. Worst-case page latency after a sell-only pass missed
    at T0 is  T0 + (B - C) + I + D  with B = 30 (pinned strategy-104
    execution.software_stops.max_staleness_minutes), C = 12 (sell-only loop
    cadence, com.renquant.intraday104), I = 10 (this StartInterval, 600 s),
    D = page delivery (measured by the test-fire drill): STALE flips 18 min
    after the first missed pass and the first page lands at ~18-28 min + D,
    against the design's page within 15 min
    (doc/design/2026-07-02-s-frac-fractional-v2.md, Alert-to-recovery SLA).
    OPEN DECISION ITEM - two ways to comply, neither chosen here:
      (a) lower max_staleness_minutes in the strategy-104 config (a
          production-config write, so its own LONG-ledger row): B - C + I
          within 15 gives B at most 17 at this 10-min interval, or B at most
          22 with the interval shortened to 5 min (StartInterval 300); or
      (b) an explicit operator exception accepting the measured envelope,
          per the design's sign-off clause.
    Until one of them lands this job is NOT eligible to install and does NOT
    count as step-5 evidence for the software_stops config row.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.renquant.stops-liveness</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/renhao/git/github/renquant-orchestrator-run/scripts/stops_liveness_pager.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/renhao/.renquant/ops/stops-liveness/launchd.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/renhao/.renquant/ops/stops-liveness/launchd.err.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin</string>
        <!-- Explicit operator configuration (deploy-plist convention set by
             Codex r2 on #460 / deploy/com.renquant.shadow-ab-daily.plist):
             the paging topic is configuration owned by this plist and
             reviewed at arming time. "renquant" is the LIVE ops topic — the
             same channel the live sell-only loop (umbrella
             scripts/intraday_sell_104.sh NTFY_TOPIC) alerts on. -->
        <key>RENQUANT_STOPS_PAGER_NTFY_TOPIC</key>
        <string>renquant</string>
        <!-- RUNTIME CONTRACT: the wrapper script has NO default interpreter
             or data root (Codex r2 on #460 / this package's 2026-07-11
             re-review) — both are explicit, reviewed arming-time
             configuration here, never a hardcoded default in the script. -->
        <!-- Same interpreter the live pipeline stack already runs under
             (the conda env RenQuant/.venv/bin/python symlinks to),
             referenced directly, NOT through the umbrella .venv path.
             Verified live 2026-07-11: the BARE conda interpreter suffices
             because the wrapper puts the checker's full first-party import
             closure (common/base-data/artifacts/model/pipeline/execution)
             on PYTHONPATH from the runtime inventory - only the third-party
             scientific stack comes from this env; none of the umbrella
             venv's editable installs are needed. -->
        <key>RENQUANT_STOPS_PAGER_PYTHON</key>
        <string>/Users/renhao/miniconda3/envs/renquant/bin/python</string>
        <!-- NEUTRAL runtime-state root — the target-state convention defined
             by renquant_orchestrator.software_stops_registry_contract
             (mirrors deployment_manifest.deploy_state_root). The checker
             looks for the registry file under this path. PREREQUISITE:
             the sell-only loop writer must be migrated to stamp here
             (renquant-execution#29 + writer R-PIN landing) BEFORE this
             plist is armed; until then the checker finds no file and
             exits STALE (correct fail-closed). This plist is DARK/staged
             only (not installed) so the false-STALE never fires. -->
        <key>RENQUANT_STOPS_PAGER_DATA_ROOT</key>
        <string>/Users/renhao/.renquant/runtime/software-stops</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
